# Names under $HOME to keep across container rebuilds, one per line
# (# starts a comment). Each becomes a symlink
#   $HOME/<name> -> afw-container/home/<name>
# Run ../container-custom.sh after editing (or just rebuild).
#
# Prefer directories. A tool that saves a file by writing a temporary file
# and renaming it replaces the symlink with a plain file; afw-container/bashrc
# warns at shell start when that happens.
#
# Do not list what the image or VS Code owns: .vscode-server*, .local,
# .cache, .npm, .profile, .bashrc, .gitconfig (VS Code copies the host's in).
# Do not list a path the devcontainer mounts a volume on (it cannot be linked).
#
# Uncomment what you use.

# afw CLI history and settings
#.afw
#.afw_history

# GitHub CLI login (gh auth login writes here)
#.config/gh

# Personal scripts
#bin

# Claude Code: settings, memory, sessions, and its main state file
#.claude
#.claude.json

# Cursor
#.cursor
